{
 "manufacturer": "Swegon",
 "manufacturer_slug": "swegon",
 "model": "SuperWISE (generation 1) BACnet IP - system objects",
 "model_slug": "superwise-gen1-bacnet-ip-system",
 "aliases": [
  "SuperWISE",
  "Super WISE",
  "WISE gen 1",
  "GB.BACnetSuper WISE.140603",
  "SuperWISE_BACnet_list_ver_1.3"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Other equipment (demand-controlled ventilation system controller)",
 "applies_to": "Swegon SuperWISE (first generation) system controllers for WISE demand-controlled ventilation, program version 1.25.",
 "summary": "SuperWISE gen 1 is the system controller of Swegon's WISE demand-controlled ventilation system and acts as a BACnet IP server (B-ASC) on its Ethernet port. Its EDE workbook gives fixed system objects (instances 65000 and up): summed supply/extract airflow per zone, the duct-pressure optimisation link to the GOLD air handler, demand flags, alarms, clock and commands. Room, damper and router objects come from per-product sheets whose instances are calculated from the zone, damper and room numbers.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "SuperWISE program version 1.25 (BACnet list ver. 1.3, 2014)",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Taken from the LOCAL sheet of SuperWISE_BACnet_list_ver_1.3.xls in Swegon's SuperWISE gen 1 BACnet zip (EDE layout). The sheet gives no settable column, so access is inferred: AVs as writable, AIs as read-only.",
  "The workbook's per-product sheets (CONTROL Za, Router, CONTROL Ra A3/A4, W1/W3/W4, ADAPT Master/Slave/WBCS, A1) calculate instances from zone (0-9), damper or branch (1-8) and room (1-60) numbers; those objects are not listed here.",
  "The Optimize sheet in the same workbook repeats some LOCAL objects but shows CoolDemandFlag/HeatDemandFlag at 65054/65055 instead of 65055/65056; the LOCAL sheet values are used.",
  "AI and AV objects share some instance numbers (65000-65005); they are different objects."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Read the per-zone summed airflows and SumAlarm (AI 65101) and the cooling/heating demand flags. The AV 65200 range is the pressure-optimisation link with the air handler: the AHU (or BMS) writes the real SA/EA pressures and running state, and SuperWISE returns the requested pressures (AI 65041/65042).",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AV 65215",
    "name": "WISE_DriftON",
    "why": "Write 1 while the AHU runs, 0 when stopped"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 65216",
    "name": "WISE_FireAlarm",
    "why": "Fire alarm; 1 forces all regulators to emergency mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 65200",
    "name": "WISE_SA_Pa",
    "why": "Real supply duct pressure from the AHU, Pa"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 65201",
    "name": "WISE_EA_Pa",
    "why": "Real extract duct pressure from the AHU, Pa"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 65221",
    "name": "AlarmReset",
    "why": "Alarm reset (returns to 0)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 65041",
    "name": "WISE_SA_ForcPa",
    "why": "Requested supply duct pressure for the AHU, Pa"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 65042",
    "name": "WISE_EA_ForcPa",
    "why": "Requested extract duct pressure for the AHU, Pa"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 65055",
    "name": "CoolDemandFlag",
    "why": "Any room needs cooling"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 65056",
    "name": "HeatDemandFlag",
    "why": "Any room needs heating"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 65101",
    "name": "SumAlarm",
    "why": "Any active alarm"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BACnet IP must be switched on in the SuperWISE Admin/Misc tab before the objects respond.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet IP on the Ethernet port (E), directly or through a switch; settings in SuperWISE Admin/Misc.",
   "Read input register (relative address 2) of a room controller to see which product sheet applies (8 CONTROL Za, 13 Router, 6 CONTROL Ra A3, 10 W4, 1 W3, 2 W1, 11/12/15 ADAPT)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "AlarmReset, RC_ForceScan and Reboot (AV 65221/65224/65225) are one-shot commands; AV 65225 = 1 reboots the server.",
   "AlarmClear (AV 65242) can delete the alarm history; 2 clears all."
  ]
 },
